{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculus"],"declarations":26,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.sumOp_residual_even_part_dead","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.sumOp_residual_even_part_dead","kind":"theorem","line":368,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.lean#L368-L381","doc":"The general-sum form: for any finite sum split into even and odd shifts, the\nresidual forces the even part off the tower. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.twoOp_residual_from_level_kills_residue_beyond","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.twoOp_residual_from_level_kills_residue_beyond","kind":"theorem","line":350,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.lean#L350-L366","doc":"**Asymptotic residual, per-level exclusivity.** If the two-term derivative-like\ntower alternates only from level `n₀` on, the residue slot is dead at every\nlevel `≥ n₀ + 2` — no seed hypothesis — while levels `2 … n₀ + 1` keep the\n`twoOp_iterate_residue` formula and are generically alive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.shiftOne_iterate_residue_zero_of_two_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.shiftOne_iterate_residue_zero_of_two_le","kind":"theorem","line":336,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.lean#L336-L348","doc":"A shift-1 iterate of length `≥ 2` has a dead residue slot for **every**\nseed — the `i = 1` factor of the iterate is `c₁(−1) = 0`. (The `#6474` lemma\n`residue_slot_zero_shift_one` needs a power-series seed only for lengths `0`\nand `1`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.residual_from_level_tower_is_odd_part","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.residual_from_level_tower_is_odd_part","kind":"theorem","line":314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.lean#L314-L333","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.twoOp_residual_kills_residue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.twoOp_residual_kills_residue","kind":"theorem","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.lean#L283-L298","doc":"**The residual kills the residue.** For the two-term derivative-like operator\n(shift-1 component annihilating constants) on a power-series fixed-parity seed, a\ntower carrying the full `(−1)^n` residual is the pure shift-1 tower, and its\nresidue slot is dead at every level. Residue and residual are mutually exclusive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.residual_tower_is_odd_part","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.residual_tower_is_odd_part","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.lean#L245-L281","doc":"**A tower carrying the full `(−1)^n` residual is generated by its odd part\nalone.** For `D = E + O` with `E` monodromy-even and `O` monodromy-odd, both\nhomogeneous, if `mono (Dⁿ X) = (−1)ⁿ ε · Dⁿ X` for every `n` (with `ε ≠ 0`), then\nat every level `Dⁿ X = Oⁿ X` and `E (Oⁿ X) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.even_part_dead_of_flip","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.even_part_dead_of_flip","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.lean#L222-L243","doc":"**Core step.** If `Z` has monodromy eigenvalue `ε' ≠ 0` and `(E + O) Z` has\neigenvalue `−ε'`, then `E Z = 0`: the even part contributes `+ε' · E Z` to\n`mono ((E + O) Z)` and the odd part `−ε' · O Z`, so flipping the sign needs\n`2ε' · E Z = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.jacksonPlusQddz_iterate_residue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.jacksonPlusQddz_iterate_residue","kind":"theorem","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.lean#L204-L213","doc":"The same `−1` weight: `[−1]_q · [1]_q = −1` whenever `[1]_q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.qIntBalZ_one_of","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.qIntBalZ_one_of","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.lean#L201-L202","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.jacksonPlusQddz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.jacksonPlusQddz","kind":"def","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.lean#L197-L199","doc":"Jackson `D_{q,t}` (shift 1, `[e+1]_q`) plus the q-deformed `d/dz` (shift 2, `[e+2]_q`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.classicalTwo_iterate_residue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.classicalTwo_iterate_residue","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.lean#L185-L191","doc":"Classical instance: `(1/t)d/dt` (shift 2, `e + 2`) plus `d/dt` (shift 1, `e + 1`).\nWeight `(−2 + 1)·(−1 + 2) = −1`. The revival is not a q-phenomenon. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.twoOp_iterate_residue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.twoOp_iterate_residue","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.lean#L170-L183","doc":"**The residue revives at level 2 and beyond.** With both components\nannihilating constants, the residue slot at level `n + 2` is the `t¹` coefficient\nof the level-`n` jet, weighted by `c₁(−2) · c₂(−1)`. No hypothesis on the seed is\nneeded: the killing slot `t⁰` is jumped over by the word (shift 1, then shift 2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.twoOp_residue_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.twoOp_residue_one","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.lean#L164-L168","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.twoOp_residue_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.twoOp_residue_zero","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.lean#L159-L162","doc":"At levels `0` and `1` the residue slot is still dead on a power-series seed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.twoOp_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.twoOp_apply","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.lean#L156-L157","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.twoOp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.twoOp","kind":"def","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.lean#L152-L154","doc":"`twoOp c₁ c₂ = shiftOp 2 c₂ + shiftOp 1 c₁`: an even and an odd derivative-like\ncomponent. Written even-part-first so that it is literally `E f + O f`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.sumOp_anticomm_mono_of_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.sumOp_anticomm_mono_of_odd","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.lean#L138-L148","doc":"A sum of odd shifts anti-commutes with the covering monodromy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.sumOp_comm_mono_of_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.sumOp_comm_mono_of_even","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.lean#L126-L136","doc":"A sum of even shifts commutes with the covering monodromy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.sumOp_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.sumOp_comp","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.lean#L115-L124","doc":"**Sums compose**: the composite of two sums is the double sum of the composed\nsymbols `shiftOp (k + l) (c k · d l (· + k))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.sumOp_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.sumOp_smul","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.lean#L109-L113","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.sumOp_residue_slot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.sumOp_residue_slot","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.lean#L105-L107","doc":"The residue slot of a sum is the sum of the slots. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.sumOp_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.sumOp_apply","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.lean#L102-L103","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.sumOp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.sumOp","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.lean#L97-L100","doc":"A finite sum of shift operators — the general q-D-module element on the\ncoefficient model: shifts `ks`, multiplier `c k` for the term of shift `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.mono_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.mono_sum","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.lean#L88-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.mono_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.mono_smul","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.lean#L85-L86","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.mono_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.mono_add","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RamifiedShiftCalculusSum.lean#L82-L83","signatureChunk":0}]}